From 184a1d2476918ebde03cf6c6ea4f2d1a109d178c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zahary Karadjov <zahary@agent-harbor.com>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 20:21:13 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] test(vm2): AVM_REACTOR, a standalone avm.wasm reactor and its
 msgpack host ABI

Adds an optional, default-off AVM_REACTOR build producing avm.wasm: one
WebAssembly module carrying vm2_sim and world_state_reference and nothing
else, with no main. It is a WASI reactor, initialised through _initialize and
called through an explicitly listed export set.

The host ABI reuses the generated msgpack schemas rather than inventing an
encoding: AvmFastSimulationInputs and AvmProvingInputs in, TxSimulationResult
out, and the two host interfaces (ContractDBInterface's eight methods,
LowLevelMerkleDBInterface's fourteen) exposed as exports over resident
implementations, so the module's import surface stays WASI-only.

avm_msgpack_coverage enumerates every crossed type by round-tripping it, for
x86-64 and for wasm32-wasip1 from one translation unit. avm_differential grows
a reactorinputs mode that prints the msgpack blobs a host needs to drive the
module, lifted from the simulator's own hint output rather than recomputed.

An unpruned control target links the same objects with --export-dynamic and
without --gc-sections, so the size effect of the link options is measurable
rather than asserted.
